==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*tumma}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|tõmmu}}, {{cog|et|tume}}, {{cog|izh|tumma}}, {{cog|krl|tumma}}, {{cog|vro|tummõ}} and {{cog|vot|tummõ}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p}}

===Adjective===
{{fi-adj|tumm|empi|in}}

# [[dark]] {{gloss|of colour}}
#: {{ant|fi|vaalea|valjakka|kirkas}}
#: {{ux|fi|Hänellä on '''tumma''' tukka.|t=She has '''dark''' hair.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Minä käytän vain '''tummia''' vaatteita.|I only wear '''dark''' clothes.}}
# [[dark-haired]]
#: {{syn|fi|tummatukkainen|tummahiuksinen|brunette|brune}}
#: {{ant|fi|vaalea|blondi}}
#: {{ux|fi|Naapurin jätkä seurustelee taas sen '''tumman''' tytön kanssa.|t=|The guy next door is dating the '''dark-haired''' girl again.}}

====Usage notes====
* The compound names of dark variants of a color are formed with genitive of {{m|fi||tumma}}, other adjectives often with nominative, depending on the head word, e.g.:
:: {{m|fi|keltainen|'''tumman'''keltainen|dark yellow}}
:: {{m|fi|tummaihoinen|'''tumma'''ihoinen|dark-skinned}}

